title: 'Decided by Jeff: a replaced root shows its own containers folder, as a fresh view of it would.'
pid: e7b8e4fd-3a44-4a48-a6a4-8865b53e4d47
body: |2-
  The first build left the original's folder under the replacement,
  each member drawn noWarrant. Told so, Jeff wrote: "Let's replace it
  with one that's accurate." Since 2026-11-14, whenever 'substitute_roots'
  re-points a root to another node, the old folder vanishes and the root
  asks for a containers folder anew ('redraw_containers_folder' in
  'server/refresh/visit.rs'), which the requests rung of the same visit
  draws: what contains the node now shown, but its view-ancestors, or no
  folder where nothing does. Switching back draws the original's again,
  the same way. Consequences, each decided:
  - The folder and its members get new viewnode IDs at every switch;
    point inside the folder moves to the root.
  - A root whose folder the user had removed gets one again: the view
    was drawn for another node.
  - Only the containers folder. Any other folder the old root held
    (subscribee, mentioners, aliases) stays, the old node's members in
    it drawn noWarrant, and the replacement's default subscribee folder
    is not added. Jeff asked only about the containers folder; the rest
    is the same fault, and the same fix would mend it.
